      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(security): bound hashFileContentsSync in approval script operand reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`hashFileContentsSync` in `src/node-host/invoke-system-run-plan.ts` reads the entire file synchronously into memory with no size limit to compute a SHA-256 hash for approval fingerprinting. A user who runs `node ./10GB-script.js` as a `system.run` operand would cause Node to block the event loop and OOM the process before approval is even evaluated.\n\nThis is a security OOM vector on the **hot approval path**:\n- Called every `system.run` to fingerprint the script operand for approval binding (line 936)\n- Called again on every revalidation before execution (line 1020)\n- File path is derived from user-supplied CLI argv — an attacker who controls the workspace can trivially OOM\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUnbounded sync `readFileSync` on user-controlled paths is a known OOM vector. The `@openclaw/fs-safe` package provides `readRegularFileSync` which enforces `maxBytes` before allocating the buffer. This fix applies that bound to `hashFileContentsSync`.\n\nAdditionally, the try-catch in `resolveMutableFileOperandSnapshotSync` now returns a proper error message (`\"approval script operand is too large or not a regular file\"`) instead of letting the throw propagate as an unhandled exception.\n\n## What Changed\n\n**`src/node-host/invoke-system-run-plan.ts`:**\n- Added import for `readRegularFileSync` from `../infra/regular-file.js`\n- Added `MAX_APPROVAL_SCRIPT_FILE_BYTES` constant (8 MiB) — script operands are code files, not data dumps\n- Replaced unbounded `fs.readFileSync(filePath)` with `readRegularFileSync({ filePath, maxBytes: MAX_APPROVAL_SCRIPT_FILE_BYTES })`\n- Wrapped the `hashFileContentsSync` call in `resolveMutableFileOperandSnapshotSync` with try-catch to return `{ ok: false, message }` instead of an unhandled throw\n\n**`src/node-host/invoke-system-run-plan.test.ts`:**\n- Added test: rejects file operand exceeding 8 MiB cap (8 MiB + 1 byte)\n- Added test: accepts file operand exactly at 8 MiB cap, verifies valid SHA-256\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `node ./10GB-script.js` -> OOM, process killed | `node ./10GB-script.js` -> rejected with \"too large or not a regular file\" |\n| `node ./4MB-script.js` -> works (unchanged) | `node ./4MB-script.js` -> works (unchanged) |\n| Error from oversized file -> unhandled exception | Error -> proper `SYSTEM_RUN_DENIED` message |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 92 existing + new tests pass:**\n\n```\n[test] src/node-host/invoke-system-run-plan.test.ts (20 tests) ✓\n[test] src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts (72 tests) ✓\n```\n\n**New boundary tests:**\n\n1. **Oversize rejection**: Creates an 8 MiB + 1 byte file and verifies `resolveMutableFileOperandSnapshotSync` returns `{ ok: false, message: \"SYSTEM_RUN_DENIED: approval script operand is too large or not a regular file\" }`\n2. **Boundary acceptance**: Creates an exactly 8 MiB file and verifies the snapshot sha256 matches a direct sha256 of the file contents",
